  "agent_dx_observations": [
    "Header ergonomics: stateless POST /mcp works directly with standard Authorization and Content-Type: application/json headers (no Accept: text/event-stream or stateful initialize handshake required), and X-Gateway-Mode-Decision transparently explains routing (observed: 'auto->codemode (score=100.0): Avg payload 17020 bytes risks prompt overflow').",
    "search_tools typed Python stubs: immediately surfaced exact region-prefixed billing tool names (billing_legacy_eu__list_eu_invoices and billing_legacy_us__list_us_invoices instead of generic list_invoices) and full return dict shapes (rows vs invoices), enabling first-try asyncio.gather execution inside Monty.",
    "Payload duplication trade-off: tools/call and search_tools responses populate both result.content[0].text (serialized JSON) and result.structuredContent, roughly doubling small JSON-RPC response sizes\u2014making Code Mode only modestly smaller on tiny 3-row single-tool queries (trial_balance_audit) while delivering huge byte/token savings on 200-row bulk joins.",
    "Stub typing quirk: nullable OpenAPI string params rendered as 'status: Any | None = None' on billing tools whereas the native MCP ledger tool rendered 'status: str | None = None'.",
    "Error clarity: RBAC denial returned a clean JSON-RPC -32003 error ('Caller lacks required role for snowflake_ledger'), and require_grounding=true returned UngroundedResultError flagging the exact fabricated ID ('CUST-9999') with subcall_count=0."
